 ],
 "literal": "The forest dweller with a curved bow and short-bladed arrows / chased away the angry-eyed elephant that ate from the field. / Along with the parakeets chased away by women wearing fragrant foliage, / that elephant dreams on the small hill in the country of the lord of the hills. / To end the distress of his humble request, / what if we reveal our secret, O friend?",
 "translation": "The forest hunter, armed with a curved bow and short arrows, chased away the angry-eyed elephant that had fed on the millet field. That elephant now sleeps on a small hill, dreaming of the parakeets that are chased away by women wearing fragrant leaf-garments. Such is the mountain country of our lord. O friend, what would happen if we reveal our secret love to our family, so that the distress of his humble, persistent pleading may finally end?",
 "modern": "வளைந்த வில்லையும் சிறிய அம்புகளையும் உடைய கானவன், தினைப்புனத்தை மேய்ந்துவிட்டு நின்ற கோபமான கண்களைக் கொண்ட யானையை விரட்டினான். அந்த யானை, நறுமணமிக்க தழையாடை அணிந்த பெண்கள் விரட்டும் கிளிகளோடு சேர்ந்து, ஒரு சிறிய குன்றின் மேல் படுத்துக் கனவு காண்கிறது. அத்தகைய மலைநாட்டை உடையவன் நம் தலைவன். தோழியே! அவனது பணிவான வேண்டுதலால் உண்டாகும் துன்பம் நீங்குமாறு, நம்முடைய களவு ஒழுக்கத்தை வீட்டில் உள்ளோரிடம் வெளிப்படுத்தினால் என்ன?",
 "explanation": "In this Kuriñci poem, the friend (தோழி) speaks to the heroine (தலைவி) about revealing their secret love to the family (அறத்தொடு நிற்றல்). The hero has been visiting secretly and making humble, submissive requests for marriage, which causes him great distress due to the difficulties of the journey. The friend describes the hero's mountain country where an elephant, chased away from the millet field by a hunter, sleeps on a small hill and dreams of the parakeets chased by women. This image of the elephant dreaming of the parakeets mirrors the hero, who is kept away from his beloved but constantly dreams of her. By revealing their secret ('மறை'), they can put an end to his distress ('வருத்தம்') and pave the way for a formal, happy marriage.",
